This network revolves around Advanced Fab, supported by a Fulfillment Hub, with inbound supply coming from ElectroParts, GlassCore Ltd., NanoMaterials Inc., FastChip Corp., and PolymerSource. The plant works with two basic inputs, lithium_cell and solder_paste, and turns them into several built-up components before shipping finished goods. In the bill of materials, each battery_pack uses 2 units of solder_paste, each cooling_unit uses 2 units of lithium_cell, and each power_module uses 3 units of solder_paste. On the finished side, a tablet requires 1 unit of lithium_cell and 1 unit of solder_paste, a smartphone is assembled from 2 units of battery_pack, 2 units of power_module, and 3 units of cooling_unit, and an FPGA uses 2 units of cooling_unit plus 2 units of battery_pack. Lithium_cell is sourced on an as-needed basis, with inventory reviewed every 8 hours and a holding charge of $9.403 per unit. Solder_paste, by contrast, is replenished on a regular cycle, with batch quantities averaging 44328.0 units and varying by about 11207.0 units, and deliveries arriving somewhere between 12.0 hours and 24.0 hours. Starting stocks are substantial: 2184390 units of battery_pack, 400509 units of cooling_unit, 2449184 units of power_module, 3434938 units of tablet, 261475 units of smartphone, and 1350875 units of FPGA. Battery_pack is reviewed every 1 hour and carries a shortage penalty of $1.452 per unit, cooling_unit is also reviewed every 1 hour with a much steeper shortage cost of $20.619 per unit, tablet inventory is checked every 1 hour with holding cost of $6.5 per unit and shortage cost of $7.725 per unit, smartphone is reviewed every 1 hour with holding cost of $5.656 per unit and shortage cost of $46.165 per unit, and FPGA is reviewed every 1 hour with a shortage cost of $8.476 per unit. Supplier terms are quite mixed. ElectroParts provides lithium_cell with a fixed 17.0-hour lead time at $116.651 per unit, payment due 10.0 days after delivery, and can supply up to 525852 units per order; shipments from ElectroParts to Advanced Fab take between 3.0 hours and 4.0 hours. NanoMaterials Inc. is another lithium_cell source, with lead time ranging from 2.0 hours to 22.0 hours, a unit cost of $499.346, payment terms between 13.0 days and 19.0 days, capacity of 525313 units, and transfer time to Advanced Fab between 4.0 hours and 6.0 hours. PolymerSource also sells lithium_cell, with an exponential lead time averaging 6.0 hours, a very low cost of $8.164 per unit, net 89.0 days payment, and a maximum order size of 72607 units. For solder_paste, GlassCore Ltd. delivers in 14.0 to 27.0 hours at $417.223 per unit, with 9.0-day payment terms and capacity capped at 826522 units, while FastChip Corp. supplies with an exponential lead time averaging 8.0 hours at $459.185 per unit and payment due between 15.0 days and 23.0 days. At Advanced Fab, tablet production is handled through a molding step that consumes lithium_cell and solder_paste and produces tablet output in a 7.0-hour to 24.0-hour cycle, using the Laser Cutter. That Laser Cutter has capacity for 5 units at a time, works with an exponential service time averaging 4.65 hours, and costs $6.586 per hour to run. Smartphone output is built in an assembly operation using battery_pack, power_module, and cooling_unit, with each cycle taking between 16.0 hours and 17.0 hours. FPGA production runs through a cutting step using cooling_unit and battery_pack, and that cycle ranges from 5.0 hours to 10.0 hours. Another shared asset in the system is the Quality Scanner, which has capacity for 3 units, a fixed 4.82-hour service time, and batch processing turned on at 47 units with a maximum wait of 14.812 hours. It is also failure-prone: uptime is exponentially distributed with a mean of 123.117 hours, downtime is a constant 21.849 hours, and operating cost is $14.959 per hour. Finished tablets, smartphones, and FPGA units move from Advanced Fab to the Fulfillment Hub for outbound fulfillment. On the demand side, HP Enterprise buys tablet, placing orders between every 9.0 hours and 42.0 hours for a constant 1711357.0 units, expecting delivery in exactly 20.0 hours. If stock is short, those orders are backordered, and the selling price is $4218.337 per unit, with customer payment arriving between 48.0 days and 61.0 days. Siemens Digital purchases smartphone with order arrivals averaging 56.0 hours, order sizes ranging from 2068951.0 units to 2120793.0 units, and customer lead time between 16.0 hours and 20.0 hours. This account runs on a partial shipment policy: available units are shipped and the rest is lost. Smartphones sell to Siemens Digital at $2008.269 per unit, and payment comes 29.0 days after delivery. NXP Semiconductors orders FPGA every 45.0 hours, each order being exactly 2959533.0 units, with promised delivery in 10.0 to 12.0 hours. Here the company ships what it has and backorders the remainder, and the sales price is $3763.449 per unit with payment due 14.0 days later. The full model runs for a horizon of 730 hours, with 10 replications.

