sin, and SoC are all managed inventories for the SoC side of the operation, while circuit_board, memory_chip, and GPU are managed for the GPU line. The SoC manufacturing step is called polishing; it takes exactly 26.0 days per cycle and consumes resin, solder_paste, memory_chip, and circuit_board to produce SoC. The GPU step is coating, running at a fixed 8.0 days per cycle and converting circuit_board plus memory_chip into GPU. There is also a Packaging Machine available with capacity for 4 units at a time, a service time ranging from 5.591 to 5.741 days, and an operating cost of $17.939 per day. Inventory levels start high: 3056394 units of circuit_board, 4989953 units of SoC, and 1549293 units of GPU. Carrying circuit_board costs $3.817 per unit, shortages cost $43.043 per unit, and it is checked every 1 day. SoC inventory costs $7.172 per unit to hold with a 1 day review cycle, while GPU holding cost is $5.803 per unit with reviews every 1 day as well. On the demand side, Apple Supply buys SoC on a steady 56.0 day ordering rhythm, with order volume averaging 1023569.0 units and varying by about 55048.0 units. Shipments to Apple Supply take exactly 28.0 days, the product sells at $270.023 per unit, and payment comes back in 52.0 to 60.0 days. If SoC stock is short, available units are shipped immediately and the remainder is backordered. Sony Electronics purchases GPU with arrivals averaging 31.0 days, and its demand is roughly 85928.0 units with variability of 17135.0 units. GPU orders are delivered in 15.0 to 16.0 days, sold at $1204.684 per unit, and paid in 45.0 to 48.0 days, with a full backorder policy when supply is not immediately available. The whole setup is evaluated over a 500 day horizon with 10 replications.

