its available per order. Plastic_pellet is handled differently, arriving in scheduled lots of 40944.0 units every 21.0 days; shortages are charged at $34.63 per unit and inventory is checked every 29 days. MegaSupply supports that flow with a consistent 4.0-day supplier lead time, a cost of $497.048 per unit, payment terms ranging from 17.0 to 78.0 days, and a maximum delivery size of 185377 units. Ceramic_substrate is sourced on demand rather than to a preset stock rule, and Process Go. supplies it with an exponential lead time averaging 14.0 days, a purchase cost of $405.292 per unit, 57.0-day payment terms, and capacity for 916531 units per order. Inside the plant, the Integration Center manages circuit_board, display_panel, ceramic_substrate, lithium_cell, resin, SoC, and plastic_pellet inventory. It starts with 3316372 units of display_panel on hand, 390884 units of circuit_board, and 893569 units of finished SoC. Circuit_board inventory carries a holding cost of $8.189 per unit and is reviewed every 1 day, while SoC inventory costs $9.187 per unit to hold and is also reviewed every 1 day. Final assembly at the Integration Center uses the Assembly Line, which has capacity for 1 unit, runs with a constant service time of 5.978 days, and costs $1.847 per day to operate. The assembly step itself takes exactly 25.0 days per cycle and combines lithium_cell, plastic_pellet, resin, ceramic_substrate, display_panel, and circuit_board into SoC output. On the demand side, NXP Semiconductors places SoC orders with exponentially distributed arrivals averaging 28.0 days, with each order ranging uniformly from 2930002.0 units to 2973892.0 units. Their promised delivery time is 21.0 days, the selling price is $4183.093 per unit, payment comes exactly 8.0 days later, and the service rule is partial fulfillment with the remainder backordered. HP Enterprise orders less frequently, every 56.0 days flat, and demand is centered around 4541241.0 units with variability of 1231375.0 units. Its customer lead time is 15.0 days, the SoC sells there for $2731.625 per unit, payment is received after 47.0 days, and if stock is unavailable the sale is lost. Broadcom Limited orders every 46.0 days, with request sizes anywhere from 1654872.0 units to 4435884.0 units; delivery commitments range from 6.0 to 18.0 days, the price is $603.18 per unit, payment arrives in 52.0 to 65.0 days, and any unmet demand is backordered. The model runs for a horizon of 365 days, with 10 replications.

