ribution. Customer demand is substantial. Apple Supply buys CPU, placing orders every 7.0 to 57.0 weeks for between 2058709.0 and 2415438.0 units, with delivery to the customer taking 3.0 weeks. If CPUs are unavailable, orders are backordered, the selling price is $581.332 per unit, and cash is collected 87.0 days later. Broadcom Limited buys tablet, with orders arriving exponentially with an average of 14.0 weeks and demand typically around 3932825.0 units with variability of about 553755.0 units. Tablet shipments take 13.0 to 13.0 weeks, available units go out immediately and the remainder is backordered, the sales price is $1569.16 per unit, and customer payment lands between 35.0 and 65.0 days. Structurally, ChipCo, FastChip Corp., and ElectroParts all feed the Integration Center, and the Integration Center sends both CPU and tablet to the Fulfillment Hub. The model runs in weeks over a 365-week planning horizon with 10 replications.

