er unit for smartphone, with all three reviewed every 1 day. Smartphone inventory also carries a shortage penalty of $27.542 per unit. On the demand side, Apple Supply buys CPU, placing orders every 56.0 days, with demand centered around 1208647.0 units and varying by about 115570.0 units. CPU shipments to Apple Supply take exactly 25.0 days, sell at $4908.083 per unit, and customer payment comes in between 27.0 days and 30.0 days. If CPU is unavailable, the sale is lost. Lenovo Group purchases smartphone, with orders arriving anywhere from 12.0 days to 54.0 days apart and demand averaging 1579159.0 units with variability of 101103.0 units. Smartphone orders are delivered in exactly 12.0 days, sold at $3590.727 per unit, and paid in 7.0 to 25.0 days; any unmet smartphone demand is backordered until stock is available. Overall, the model includes GlobalComponents and BatteryTech feeding Advanced Fab, Advanced Fab, Fab, and Fulfillment Hub as the operating sites, and it runs over a 500-day horizon with 1 replication.

