 in one flow, and memory_chip, camera, and epoxy_compound in the other, after which both EV_battery and camera move on to the Warehouse. Starting stock is very large for both finished goods, with 3890870 units of EV_battery and 4745203 units of camera on hand initially. Camera inventory also has a holding cost of $6.164 per unit, a shortage cost of $38.934 per unit, and a review cycle of 1 day. On the demand side, NXP Semiconductors buys EV_battery, placing orders with an average gap of 17.0 days. Order size is approximately 582083.0 units, varying by about 81548.0 units, and delivery to that customer takes exactly 16.0 days. If inventory is short, available units are shipped and the remaining demand is lost. The selling price is $2110.239 per unit, and payment comes 64.0 days after delivery. Broadcom Limited purchases camera, with orders arriving anywhere from 12.0 days to 21.0 days apart, and each order is fixed at 1800984.0 units. Camera shipments reach the customer in 6.0 days, unmet demand is lost, the sales price is $1815.502 per unit, and customer payment is received after 29.0 days. The model runs for a 500-day horizon with 1 replication.

