n holding and $9.834 per unit in shortage cost, again on a 1-hour review rhythm. Finished goods begin with 1796746 units of medical_device, where shortages cost $40.476 per unit and inventory is reviewed every 1 hour; 193213 units of EV_battery, with a shortage cost of $28.85 per unit and the same 1-hour review; and 642069 units of industrial_sensor, carrying $0.272 per unit with reviews every 1 hour. Supplier coverage is split across materials. Memory Star provides carbon_fiber with a lead time fixed in practice at 13.0 to 13.0 hours, charging $427.049 per unit, and payment falls due between 20.0 days and 37.0 days after receipt. GlobalComponents is the second carbon_fiber source, delivering in 3.0 to 18.0 hours, at $464.841 per unit, with payment terms of 18.0 to 27.0 days; its transfer to Main Factory takes 4.0 hours. Copper_wire comes from NanoMaterials Inc. or FastChip Corp. NanoMaterials Inc. ships in 11.0 to 22.0 hours, costs $226.311 per unit, allows exactly 86.0 days to pay, and needs 8.0 hours to transfer to Main Factory. FastChip Corp. averages 21.0 hours on lead time, charges $84.741 per unit, offers 19.0-day payment, can supply up to 510771 units per order, and reaches the plant in 2.0 hours. For lithium_cell, BatteryTech has a consistent 25.0-hour lead time, costs $309.031 per unit, gives 70.0-day payment terms, can supply up to 523838 units per delivery, and transfer runs between 5.0 and 10.0 hours. ElectroParts is the alternate source, with lead time between 13.0 and 20.0 hours, a much lower unit cost of $22.228, and payment due between 49.0 days and 73.0 days. Plastic_pellet is sourced from ChipCo and MetalFab Inc. ChipCo averages 27.0 hours of supplier lead time, charges $53.263 per unit, requires payment after 51.0 days, can deliver up to 90121 units, and takes 7.0 hours to move to Main Factory. MetalFab Inc. is much faster at an average of 1.0 hour, charges $53.12 per unit, and uses 58.0-day payment terms. Production is centered at Main Factory. 