 week. Finished goods flow from Plant A to the Distribution Center for medical_device and from Main Factory to the Distribution Center for EV_battery. Demand comes from two customers: Siemens Digital buys medical_device, placing orders every 18.0 to 36.0 weeks, with demand centered around 1181589.0 units and varying by about 224259.0 units; deliveries to Siemens Digital take exactly 2.0 weeks, available stock ships immediately and the remainder is backordered, the selling price is $723.242 per unit, and payment is received in 38.0 to 57.0 days. Lenovo Group purchases EV_battery on a fixed 29.0-week ordering rhythm, with demand ranging from 1078842.0 units to 1962640.0 units; customer lead time runs between 7.0 weeks and 29.0 weeks, whatever is available is shipped and the rest of the demand is lost, and the sales price is $3963.313 per unit with customer payment arriving in 53.0 to 73.0 days. The scenario is evaluated over a 100-week planning horizon, with results collected after a 50-week warm-up period.

