 also a CNC Machine in the system with capacity for 1 unit at a time, an exponentially distributed service time averaging 7.351 days, and an operating cost of $4.874 per day. On the finished goods side, drone inventory starts at 1239309 units, carries a holding cost of $2.884 per unit, faces a shortage cost of $19.192 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 day. CPU inventory starts at 1107250 units, has a shortage cost of $41.497 per unit, and is also checked every 1 day. Demand comes from 2 customers. Siemens Digital buys drone units, placing orders every 46.0 days, with demand typically around 2317553.0 units and varying by about 40041.0 units. Customer delivery takes between 17.0 days and 29.0 days, unmet demand is lost, the selling price is $793.9 per unit, and payment is received between 25.0 days and 53.0 days later. NXP Semiconductors buys CPU units with order arrivals averaging 34.0 days, order size ranging from 410249.0 units to 553918.0 units, delivery between 7.0 days and 9.0 days, and the same lost-sales approach if stock is unavailable. CPU units sell at $1107.163 per unit, and cash is collected exactly 47.0 days after delivery. The modeled network includes the 3 suppliers, the Pilot Line, and the Fulfillment Hub, and it is run over a planning horizon of 730 days with 1 replication.

