diately and the remainder is backordered. Sales to Infineon are priced at $1819.978 per unit, with payment received 7.0 days after delivery. Sony Electronics also buys CPU units, sending orders somewhere between 13.0 and 26.0 hours apart, with order sizes ranging from 554031.0 units to 1729938.0 units. Sony accepts a fixed 26.0-hour delivery time, follows a full backorder arrangement when inventory is unavailable, pays $1432.337 per unit, and settles invoices in 40.0 to 55.0 days. On the finished goods side, CPU inventory is reviewed every 1 hour, and shortages cost $10.062 per unit. The model runs for a horizon of 365 hours.

