due between 48.0 days and 57.0 days, and a maximum delivery size of 206670 units. Main Factory manages aluminum_sheet, epoxy_compound, heat_sink, solar_panel, and glass_fiber for one molding process that turns aluminum_sheet, glass_fiber, heat_sink, and epoxy_compound into solar_panel in exactly 16.0 days. The same Main Factory also manages heat_sink, aluminum_sheet, camera, and epoxy_compound for another molding step that converts epoxy_compound, heat_sink, and aluminum_sheet into camera in anywhere from 17.0 days to 29.0 days. Material flows from MetalFab Inc., MegaSupply, and Memory Star into Main Factory, and finished solar_panel and camera volumes move from Main Factory to Fulfillment Hub. On the demand side, NXP Semiconductors buys solar_panel, placing orders with exponential interarrival averaging 19.0 days; demand is roughly 4346469.0 units with variability of about 610241.0 units, customer lead time runs from 11.0 days to 20.0 days, the selling price is $1098.548 per unit, payment comes between 34.0 days and 75.0 days later, and available stock ships first with the balance backordered. HP Enterprise purchases camera with orders arriving every 30.0 days to 40.0 days, demand ranging from 1611497.0 units to 3154378.0 units, delivery promised in 1.0 days to 3.0 days, a selling price of $1162.812 per unit, and payment fixed at 73.0 days after receipt; if inventory is short, demand is fully backordered. The model runs for a 500-day horizon with 1 replication.

